    },
    {
      "id": "rDYvQOQ2AfbnJSUitxeIh",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 818.1535815332372,
      "y": -57008.03398840256,
      "width": 1138.433349609375,
      "height": 1800,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c0sh",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 612025053,
      "version": 15,
      "versionNonce": 1755754013,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1775719920838,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "====================================================\n              AWS IAM ASSIGNMENT\n====================================================\n\n\nThe goal of this exercise is to practice creating \nand managing IAM Users, Groups, Policies, and Roles \nin AWS, and to understand how permissions work.\n\n----------------------------------------------------\nTASK STEPS\n----------------------------------------------------\n\n1. Create a New IAM User\n   - Name the user: student-user\n   - Give AWS Management Console access\n   - Set a custom password\n\n   ✔ Expected: You can log in to AWS with this user.\n\n----------------------------------------------------\n\n2. Create a Group\n   - Group name: S3-ReadOnly-Group\n   - Attach the policy: AmazonS3ReadOnlyAccess\n\n   ✔ Expected: Group members can only *view* S3 buckets,\n     not create or delete them.\n\n----------------------------------------------------\n\n3. Add User to Group\n   - Add \"student-user\" to \"S3-ReadOnly-Group\"\n\n   ✔ Expected: When logged in as student-user, you can \n     list S3 buckets but cannot create/delete them.\n\n----------------------------------------------------\n\ntt",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "====================================================\n              AWS IAM ASSIGNMENT\n====================================================\n\n\nThe goal of this exercise is to practice creating \nand managing IAM Users, Groups, Policies, and Roles \nin AWS, and to understand how permissions work.\n\n----------------------------------------------------\nTASK STEPS\n----------------------------------------------------\n\n1. Create a New IAM User\n   - Name the user: student-user\n   - Give AWS Management Console access\n   - Set a custom password\n\n   ✔ Expected: You can log in to AWS with this user.\n\n----------------------------------------------------\n\n2. Create a Group\n   - Group name: S3-ReadOnly-Group\n   - Attach the policy: AmazonS3ReadOnlyAccess\n\n   ✔ Expected: Group members can only *view* S3 buckets,\n     not create or delete them.\n\n----------------------------------------------------\n\n3. Add User to Group\n   - Add \"student-user\" to \"S3-ReadOnly-Group\"\n\n   ✔ Expected: When logged in as student-user, you can \n     list S3 buckets but cannot create/delete them.\n\n----------------------------------------------------\n\ntt",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "dEDUGDgkkk5dz07Pbpxt5",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2126.879071729314,
      "y": -56765.98640351495,
      "width": 1059.2332763671875,
      "height": 1530,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c0si",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1899519805,
      "version": 38,
      "versionNonce": 1559793203,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1775719920838,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "4. Create a Custom Policy\n   - Policy name: EC2-StartStop-Only\n   - Use the following JSON:\n\n   {\n     \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n     \"Statement\": [\n       {\n         \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n         \"Action\": [\n           \"ec2:StartInstances\",\n           \"ec2:StopInstances\"\n         ],\n         \"Resource\": \"*\"\n       }\n     ]\n   }\n\n   ✔ Expected: This policy only allows starting and \n     stopping EC2 instances.\n\n----------------------------------------------------\n\n5. Create a Role for EC2\n   - Trusted entity: AWS Service → EC2\n   - Role name: EC2-S3Access-Role\n   - Attach policy: AmazonS3FullAccess\n\n   ✔ Expected: EC2 instances with this role can \n     access S3 directly without credentials.\n\n----------------------------------------------------\n\n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "4. Create a Custom Policy\n   - Policy name: EC2-StartStop-Only\n   - Use the following JSON:\n\n   {\n     \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n     \"Statement\": [\n       {\n         \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n         \"Action\": [\n           \"ec2:StartInstances\",\n           \"ec2:StopInstances\"\n         ],\n         \"Resource\": \"*\"\n       }\n     ]\n   }\n\n   ✔ Expected: This policy only allows starting and \n     stopping EC2 instances.\n\n----------------------------------------------------\n\n5. Create a Role for EC2\n   - Trusted entity: AWS Service → EC2\n   - Role name: EC2-S3Access-Role\n   - Attach policy: AmazonS3FullAccess\n\n   ✔ Expected: EC2 instances with this role can \n     access S3 directly without credentials.\n\n----------------------------------------------------\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
